[statement]
Where a package states two entries an installed package answers, through
a name it provides at a version and by its own name, the one stated last
decides: `y` needs `v`, which `x` provides at a version, and then `x`, and
apk removes `x` right after `y`. Stated the other way round, `x` goes
last (`a-package-needed-by-name-and-through-a-provided-name-is-removed-last`).

[repository]
P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:x
V:1
p:v=1

P:y
V:1
D:v x

P:z
V:1

[request]
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove y 1
remove x 1
remove z 1
install b 1
